encyclopedia :underturns do
  name "Underturns"
  kind :phenomenon
  subkind :physical_phenomenon
  status :complete
  log "2026-08-31 — Renamed Stratum Exchange to Underturns. Ravel's named Underturn already supplied the field word; the type now extends that word to the complete family of intact layer exchanges."
  topics :"fluid-reality", :mystery, :danger, :archives, :subject_bloom
  prevalence :rare
  appears_when all: { place: [:displacement_zone] }
  summary "Underturns are displacement events in which two layers of a structure trade places intact, each arriving furnished and exactly where the other used to be. Most strike once and overnight; the field at Ravel repeats on a nine-day cycle."
  medium "Layered structures in displacement country: habs, towers, terraced settlements"
  nature "A clean positional swap of two strata, complete with contents, recorded without witnesses to the transition itself"
  hazard "Every connection between the swapped layers and the building — stairs, pipes, habits — is wrong by exactly the swap, and the first hour's injuries are all people using yesterday's map"

  descriptive_identity(
    signs: "The building wakes up wrong: the stair that led to the loom room leads to the " \
           "cold store, the windows on the fifth show the third's view, and the residents " \
           "assemble in the street to count floors aloud like children doing sums.",
    effects: "The swapped strata arrive whole — furniture, stores, sleeping cats, the dust " \
             "in the corners — and every single event on record has been pairwise and " \
             "complete, with nobody awake to see the moment of exchange.",
    hazards: "Services connect by position: pipes feed the wrong kitchens, the third " \
             "floor's weight sits where the fifth's was engineered for, and displaced-room " \
             "law's tidiest chapter meets its messiest mornings."
  )

  prose <<~PROSE
    Most displacement events leave ragged joins or overlapping rooms. In an underturn, two whole layers of a structure trade places overnight. The third floor becomes the fifth; a cellar and its contents arrive at the attic level. Each stratum remains intact and level, with seamless walls and working doors, while every connection that follows position rather than the moved layer points to the wrong place. Xyloathax's registry lists eleven certain single events and the Gray Line cordon adds four. All fifteen were pairwise and complete, and nobody saw the transition, including people asleep inside the moved layers. #{ref :ravel_underturn, "Ravel Underturn"} is the one known field that repeats, and its nine-day cycle is where surveyors learned the signs: paired signal silence and instruments reporting each volume in two places at once.

    Displacement services drill for the first morning. Residents wake in familiar rooms at a different height, and most early injuries come from stairs taken by habit. Crews brace the changed load, map every landing, reconnect pipes by layer, and walk residents through the new stack twice a day for a month. Under #{encyclopedia_ref :thresholds, "threshold law"}, ownership follows the intact stratum. Surveyors record the join, contents, and testimony of sleepers because underturns repeat with a completeness that distinguishes them from other displacement events; current records establish that pattern without identifying its cause.
  PROSE

  cue "The whole building's residents stand in the street at dawn counting windows aloud, and the third floor's flower boxes bloom two storeys higher than yesterday."
  cue "Inside, a resident opens the stair door on ingrained habit, stops at a cold store that should be a loom room, and stands there recalculating with a hand still on the latch."
  affordance "An underturn moves everything and destroys nothing — the swapped strata arrive whole and habitable, ownership follows the layer under law, and the displacement services' recovery is re-mapping rather than rescue."
  pressure "Pipes, structural loads, stairs, and residents' habits remain tied to the old positions; crews brace the building, shut services, and post guides before routine movement resumes."
  variation "Xyloathax's eleven certain exchanges cluster in its Bloom-caught quarter and are commemorated by the residents with floor-warming parties in both directions."
  variation "The Gray Line's four events include the one double exchange on record — two swaps, two seasons apart, restoring the original order — which the registry files with the annotation 'resolved,' over the surveyors' written objection."
end
